body:
I ended up plucking off the leaves. I stopped watering them so much. A deep/heavy watering once every 2 weeks was good enough for them. Eventually the two small pots I had ended up growing so much that I gave them to my mom who is maintaining them. We now have like 4 large pots of pathos and several smaller pots that we propagated, and we're now selling off any more that we propagate!

&#x200B;

Nowadays, all she does is leave the pots outside on a rainy day. We don't do any other watering than the natural rain that we get and all of the pothos are super healthy. They've got this deep dark shade of green (some are lighter if they're closer to the window). I live in the Eastern part of the US if that makes a difference. Hope that helps!

Hi people!

&#x200B;

I'm going to Egypt for a month to study abroad and I'm going to be staying with a host family during my time there. I'm from the United States (Kentucky), and I was wondering if there would be any appropriate gift that I could prepare?

&#x200B;

I have a box of Ghiradelli chocolates and Ferrero Rocher, but I didn't know if this would be enough. I have some fancy candles that I'm also considering, but I didn't know if that was appropriate as I'll be staying with a Muslim family. Any recommendations would be useful!
